# Runtime state — never committed (owned by the daemon on the server)
auth/
*.sqlite
*.sock
*.log
.editord.*

# This repo holds ONLY what the editor WRITES: readlex.json and patches/.
# Everything the editor merely READS — the processed upstream corpora and the
# trained models — is staged outside git (the editor's build/staged, deployed to
# /var/lib/shaw-spell/staged). Versioning 1.1 GB of regenerable input beside a
# 1.6 MB patch store is what made a full clone unpackable on the server.
#
# The history was rewritten to drop them, so nothing below is tracked here.

# Processed upstream — staged, never committed.
supplement-*.json
definitions-latin-*.json
definitions-shavian-*.json
definitions-wiktionary.json
site-data/
hunspell/
bncfreq/

# ...EXCEPT as shards. The patterns above are unanchored, so they match at any
# depth and silently swallowed all 135 files under shards/ — `git status` showed
# nothing to add and a commit would have been empty. The pool and the definitions
# corpus ARE committed here, split into 27 per-initial shards each, because
# GitHub rejects any blob over 100 MB and a clone cannot otherwise obtain them.
#
# The negation has to name the FILES, not just the directory: git will not
# re-include a file whose own pattern still matches, so `!shards/` alone leaves
# every shard ignored. The whole-file forms at the repository root stay ignored.
!shards/*.json

# Trained models. A model is committed when nothing can rebuild it, and ignored
# when something can — the test is reproducibility, not size.
#
# The g2p pair is committed (12.4 MB) because no trainer for it exists in this
# repository, in shaw-spell, on any branch, in any worktree, or in the dangling
# commits: it was frozen into the tree from an ad-hoc training run and only the
# inference module came with it. Ignoring it would mean a clone could neither
# obtain nor rebuild a file the pipeline reads.
ipa-normalizer-model.json
rhoticity-model.pkl

# Pipeline intermediates and review scratch — regenerated on demand.
readlex-reference.tsv
wordnet-comprehensive.json
editorial*.csv
new-words-*.tsv
review-*.tsv
phrase-divergence.*
.DS_Store
